From 26.2.4. A shm-only compositor has no dmabuf feedback and no wl_drm,
so the Wayland DRM path fails. eglInitialize then clears Zink and retries
with swrast. A process that still has the zink driver selected draws
frames that never land in those wl_shm buffers.

Stay on the swrast loader while Zink remains set, so kopper presents
through Vulkan WSI. There is no DRM fd on this path, so the EGL device
is the software node; the GPU is reached through Vulkan.

diff --git a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c
@@ -3262,7 +3262,9 @@ dri2_initialize_wayland_swrast(_EGLDisplay *disp)
    if (!dri2_create_screen(disp))
       goto cleanup;
 
-   if (!dri2_setup_device(disp, disp->Options.ForceSoftware)) {
+   /* No DRM fd on the Zink shm path. The software node is the EGL device. */
+   if (!dri2_setup_device(disp,
+                          disp->Options.ForceSoftware || disp->Options.Zink)) {
       _eglError(EGL_NOT_INITIALIZED, "DRI2: failed to setup EGLDevice");
       goto cleanup;
    }
@@ -3297,7 +3299,8 @@ dri2_initialize_wayland_swrast(_EGLDisplay *disp)
 EGLBoolean
 dri2_initialize_wayland(_EGLDisplay *disp)
 {
-   if (disp->Options.ForceSoftware)
+   /* DRM init cannot succeed here. Do not let the retry clear Zink. */
+   if (disp->Options.ForceSoftware || disp->Options.Zink)
       return dri2_initialize_wayland_swrast(disp);
    else
       return dri2_initialize_wayland_drm(disp);
